// Broadside in the Ice: a merchant ship sunk by shellfire in a frozen harbour.
//
// Every ship floats on its own hull, with no pins or moorings. A body is lifted
// by the water its outline displaces below the surface, its dry hold included,
// so the merchant and the warship ride at their waterlines with their decks
// clear, and the lift moves to whichever side sits deeper, so they float
// upright. At dawn the merchant lies off a lighthouse with ice floes around her
// (ice, 90, rides nine-tenths under) and a warship beyond. The warship's first
// shot blows in her bow at the waterline: the fore hold floods to the sea's
// level and she settles by the head behind her watertight iron bulkhead.
// Grapeshot cuts down the tops of her masts, which float. Two shells amidships
// break her in two; each half floods through its broken end, tips and goes to
// the bottom with its iron ballast and the cargo in its hold, and her lanterns
// go out as the water reaches them. The same shells burst the lamp-oil tank on
// her deck and set the oil alight; burning oil stays a liquid and burns on the
// water where it spills. Scripted: the muzzle flashes and smoke, and the shell
// bursts. The floating, flooding, trim, breaking and sinking, and the fire,
// follow from them. The sea is at 0 C and the floes at -10 C; ice takes in its
// latent heat before it melts, so they last the scene.
[scene]
name = broadside in the ice
description = A warship's shells hole a merchant at the waterline, break her in two and set her lamp oil burning on the water; both halves flood and sink while her mast tops and the ice floes float.
size = 1440 644
seed = 41
ticks = 2280
wind = -1

[legend]
w wood
m metal
t torch
s stone
b brick
k basalt
x glass
O oil
. air
S snow
C concrete
c coal
I ice body temp=-10

[build]
fill 0 624 1440 644 bedrock
fill 0 200 6 644 bedrock
fill 1434 200 1440 644 bedrock
fill 6 380 1434 624 water
temp 6 380 1434 624 0
terrain 6 1434 596 6 60 sand 624
[grid 6 130]
